# ====================================================================
# Blockchain Data Monitoring Dashboard - Environment Variables Configuration
# ====================================================================
#
# Author:  Peile Wu
# Email:   peile.wu.1990@gmail.com
# Date:    July 26, 2025
# Purpose: Configure environment variables for blockchain monitoring application,
#          including RPC node connection information and server port settings
#
# Documentation:
# This configuration file defines key configuration parameters required for the
# blockchain data monitoring dashboard to connect to multiple blockchain networks
# and provide real-time data monitoring services.
# ====================================================================

# ================================
# Blockchain Network RPC Connection Configuration
# ================================
#
# RPC (Remote Procedure Call) Concept Explanation:
# RPC is a computer communication protocol that allows programs to call procedures
# or functions in another address space. In blockchain context, RPC nodes provide
# standardized API interfaces that enable developers to:
# - Query blockchain state (latest block number, account balances)
# - Send transactions to the network
# - Listen to network events
# - Retrieve historical data
#
# URL Structure: https://rpc.ankr.com/[network]/[api-key]
# - rpc.ankr.com: Free RPC service provided by Ankr
# - network: Specifies blockchain network (eth=Ethereum, polygon=Polygon)
# - api-key: Authentication key for identity verification and request rate limiting

# Ethereum Mainnet RPC Connection
# Network Type: Layer 1 (L1) - Base layer blockchain
# Network Characteristics:
# - Ethereum is the largest smart contract platform
# - Uses Proof of Work (PoW) transitioning to Proof of Stake (PoS) consensus
# - Higher transaction fees but highest security and decentralization
# - Chain ID: 1 (Unique identifier for Ethereum mainnet)
ETHEREUM_RPC_URL=https://rpc.ankr.com/eth/b2381032a6bd5ae6e19c344aa16f6c64f614da8162ed7eb91d4157af7ad6537f

# Polygon Network RPC Connection
# Network Type: Layer 2 (L2) - Sidechain/Scaling solution
# Network Characteristics:
# - Polygon is an Ethereum sidechain providing faster and cheaper transactions
# - Uses Proof of Stake (PoS) consensus mechanism
# - Fully compatible with Ethereum (EVM compatible)
# - Transaction confirmation time: ~2 seconds vs Ethereum's ~15 seconds
# - Transaction fees: Usually < $0.01 vs Ethereum's $1-50+
# - Chain ID: 137 (Unique identifier for Polygon mainnet)
# - Connected to Ethereum mainnet through state bridges ensuring asset security
POLYGON_RPC_URL=https://rpc.ankr.com/polygon/b2381032a6bd5ae6e19c344aa16f6c64f614da8162ed7eb91d4157af7ad6537f

# ================================
# Server Port Configuration
# ================================

# WebSocket Service Port
# Port Number: 8080
# Selection Rationale:
# - 8080 is a commonly used HTTP alternative port, widely allowed by firewalls
# - Does not conflict with system reserved ports (0-1023)
# - Easy to remember and configure
# - Usually not occupied by other applications
# Purpose: Provides real-time bidirectional communication, pushing blockchain data updates to clients
WEBSOCKET_PORT=8080

# HTTP Server Port
# Port Number: 3000
# Selection Rationale:
# - 3000 is the standard port in Node.js development
# - Does not conflict with system services (like 80-HTTP, 443-HTTPS)
# - Default support in development tools
# - Easy for local development and testing
# Purpose: Provides static file serving, API endpoints, and health check endpoints
HTTP_PORT=3000

# ================================
# Data Update Configuration
# ================================

# Block Data Update Interval (milliseconds)
# Setting: 5000ms (5 seconds)
# Selection Rationale:
# - Ethereum block time is ~12-15 seconds, 5-second checks can capture new blocks timely
# - Polygon block time is ~2 seconds, 5-second checks balance real-time performance and resource consumption
# - Avoids excessive API calls, preventing rate limit triggers
# - Provides sufficient buffer time for free RPC nodes
# Impact: Clients will receive blockchain state updates every 5 seconds
BLOCK_UPDATE_INTERVAL=5000

# ====================================================================
# Technical Overview
# ====================================================================
#
# L1 vs L2 Network Comparison:
#
# Layer 1 (Ethereum Mainnet):
# ✅ Advantages: Highest security, fully decentralized, most complete ecosystem
# ❌ Disadvantages: High transaction fees, low TPS (~15 TPS), slow confirmation during network congestion
#
# Layer 2 (Polygon):
# ✅ Advantages: Extremely low transaction fees, high TPS (~7000 TPS), fast confirmation
# ❌ Disadvantages: Security depends on mainnet, relatively newer technology stack
#
# Monitoring Strategy:
# By simultaneously monitoring L1 and L2 networks, we can:
# - Compare network activity across different layers
# - Analyze fund flows between different networks
# - Provide optimal transaction path recommendations for users
# - Monitor cross-chain bridge usage patterns
#
# ====================================================================
# Security Considerations
# ====================================================================
#
# 1. API Key Protection:
#    - Do not commit this file to public Git repositories
#    - Use .gitignore to exclude .env files
#    - Use dedicated API keys for production environments
#
# 2. Port Security:
#    - Production environments should use reverse proxy (e.g., Nginx)
#    - Configure firewall rules to restrict port access
#    - Use HTTPS/WSS encrypted connections
#
# 3. Rate Limiting:
#    - Monitor API call frequency to avoid exceeding limits
#    - Implement retry mechanisms and fallback strategies
#    - Consider upgrading to paid RPC services for higher limits
#
# ====================================================================